WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.000
This is our garden.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.110
My father is cultivating
some stuff like tomatoes,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.083
pumpkins, a lot of potatoes.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.423
And this is all polluted,
heavily polluted.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.660
How does it make me feel being
a neighbor of 3M company?

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.690
I don't like them being my
neighbors, but they are.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.840
I use stuff of 3M, which I don't want to,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.760
but it's just like that.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.860
I have no other option.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.480
They're everywhere.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.600
My entire family

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.470
is highly affected

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.943
by that stupid chemical.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.790
You may not realize it,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.390
but almost everyone has some level of PFAS

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:55.020
in their bloodstream because
these products are everywhere

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.640
in our everyday environment.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.860
PFAS is the umbrella term

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.040
for thousands of different
kinds of chemicals.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.110
They're known as "forever chemicals."

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:07.410
They are man-made
chemicals used in thousands

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.300
of different kinds of products.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.980
They are miraculous chemicals.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.190
You can't find a better
coating, for instance,

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.200
to make your jacket waterproof.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.810
They've made our lives
convenient in many ways.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:22.560
From the foods you eat,
to the sofa you sit on,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.707
to the rain jacket you put
on when you go outside.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.760
But the problem is they don't
degrade in the environment,

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.790
and they're almost
impossible to get rid of.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.240
They accumulate in soil,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.140
rivers, drinking water
and in the bloodstream

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.630
of people who are exposed to them.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:48.870
And now, PFAS chemicals
are associated with a range

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:53.640
of health problems: hormone
and immune disorders,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:58.170
thyroid malfunctions, but as well,

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:03.030
high cholesterol and
diabetes, kidney problems

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.033
and even a diminished vaccine efficacy.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.730
3M maintains that these
chemicals are not harmful

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.510
to human health in the levels
detected in the environment.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.940
But of course, that really depends

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.370
on where you're talking about.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.270
In some areas,

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.540
particularly around the
factories that they have,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.490
the levels detected in the
environment are incredibly high.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.660
3M is a global corporation,
a conglomerate,

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.510
that makes a wide range of products.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.240
Everything from its flagship product,

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.260
Scotchgard, to protect
fabric and your sofa.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.913
It makes Post-it notes.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.340
It makes N95 masks. But it
also makes everyday products

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.660
that are not branded.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.983
3M has billions in sales and factories

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.513
in different parts of the world.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:11.000
3M's factory is located on
the banks of the river Scheldt

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.660
in the city of Antwerp.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.353
It is part of Europe's
biggest chemical cluster.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.460
A highway separates that chemical cluster

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:24.513
from what is a suburban farming community.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.500
3M began operating in Belgium in the 1970s

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:38.870
and started making PFOS there in 1976.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:43.590
Now it stopped making PFOS there in 2002,

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.020
but in those intervening years,

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.663
it contaminated the surrounding area.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:54.590
Those people living just behind
the 3M factory were exposed

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:00.120
to the PFOS emissions from that plant,

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.600
including from the air and
the soil and the water.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.150
And it's had a really devastating impact,

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:09.153
both on the people who
live and work there.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.963
I live, let's say,

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.740
500 meters away from

00:04:22.588 --> 00:04:25.863
the chemical plant of the 3M company.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.350
I live here with my family:
three children, my husband,

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.750
my parents just across the door,

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.810
my brother across the street,

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.090
and that's me.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.840
So, we live here for

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.213
five generations long.

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.493
Then, they tell me just
like two years ago,

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:54.660
maybe it's better that your
children don't play outside

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.900
and that you clean your
house two times a week

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.160
in a really proper way.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.880
Because we know that we produce a chemical

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.730
and it's in your house,
it's in your garden,

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:07.593
and it's not good for children.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.450
I don't want to expose my
children to those chemicals.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.920
Everybody was like, move, move.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.330
And I was like, why?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.360
I already exposed them in a huge amount

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:28.320
just by holding them,
just by being pregnant,

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.210
just by feeding them.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.073
I exposed them as a mom.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:39.770
So, I breastfed my daughter
for at least a year,

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.073
six months to a year.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.140
And I was happy, it was
fine, everything was fine.

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:50.160
And suddenly, she becomes 4 years old

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.730
and not everything was fine any longer.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:54.903
She has a problem.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:00.600
According to outside world,

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.880
she's slightly disabled.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:03.713
Why?

00:06:03.713 --> 00:06:07.680
Because she had a shortness
of oxygen in her brain

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.100
and some things are not
working that well anymore.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.630
Maybe the problem is caused
by that chemical company.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:16.463
Maybe not.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:18.270
Is she dying?

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.680
No.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.910
Will she get cancer?

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:21.743
Who knows?

00:06:21.743 --> 00:06:22.576
I don't know.

00:06:22.576 --> 00:06:24.210
I don't know how bad it is, you know?

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.580
And nobody knows. Nobody.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.983
Even 3M, they say they don't know.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:34.260
But I gave her a huge, huge, huge amount

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:37.710
of that kind of chemical
because I thought,

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.780
yeah, it's good to breastfeed, why not?

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:42.720
It's easy, nice, easy,
it's nature, you know.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.720
It's just, like, yeah, what
you're supposed to do as a mom.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:49.773
I didn't do anything wrong.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.930
So, we eliminate PFAS

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.530
through loss of blood or in the urine.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:01.500
But one of the biggest
ways of eliminating PFAS

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.360
is through pregnancy and breastfeeding,

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.880
which is incredibly worrisome.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:10.200
That means that children have
some of the highest exposures

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.440
because mothers pass PFAS
from their bloodstream

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.180
onto their fetuses.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:19.860
And children are incredibly
vulnerable to contamination

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.440
because their organs are still developing,

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.633
their biochemistries are still evolving.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:28.170
Some scientists described this to me

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:31.083
as a ticking time bomb
for future generations.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.980
This contamination might
never have come to light

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:39.965
if not for a plan to build
a multi-billion-euro tunnel

00:07:39.965 --> 00:07:43.980
and highway project that was
due to pop out right next

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.923
to 3M's factory in Antwerp.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:52.830
The plan required the
digging up of tons of soil

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:55.740
and river silt and being moved

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.993
to different parts of Belgium.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:02.310
The decision to move all
this soil to other parts

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:07.310
of Flanders led activists
to start scrutinizing

00:08:07.315 --> 00:08:09.720
what's in the soil.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:14.520
And two activists came
across some documents

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:18.990
that they requested from
the state highway company

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:21.810
and from Flemish regulators and discovered

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:26.460
that the soil being dug
up near the 3M factory

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.793
was heavily contaminated with PFOS.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:35.280
In the middle of this environmental report

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.470
on the sanitation report for 3M,

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:40.500
I find what's pretty much a photocopy

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:44.474
of groundwater measurements from 2000s.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.330
And my first reflex is, like, oh,

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:52.170
there's a problem with the
decimal comma or point.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.900
You know, I was thinking, oh,
you know, they misplaced it,

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:58.830
so it's like a thousand times
too much, or it must be.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.467
But it wasn't, it was like, you know,

00:09:01.467 --> 00:09:05.940
250,000 micrograms per liter, I think.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.210
Just so staggeringly high.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:10.650
I'd never seen numbers like that,

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.350
even in, you know, these
international reports.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:18.350
And that was loose in the
groundwater underneath 3M.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:26.610
If we go by the current
data and the knowledge

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.310
from the European Food
Safety Administration,

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:33.000
they get to, like, a norm
around 4 nanograms per liter

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.620
for drinking water.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.890
Now, what we saw there
was something that was

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:42.060
in the order of a couple
hundred million times that.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.660
That's what we're talking about.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:49.440
Now this caused a chain of events

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.963
that caused a huge political scandal.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:58.260
What came out was that the
state-owned highway company

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:01.530
had done a secret deal with 3M

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:06.330
that would enable them to
deposit the most contaminated

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:10.110
and polluted soil onto 3M's factory site

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:15.000
to build what they called
a security wall on a site

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.110
that previously didn't need
any kind of security wall.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:23.340
And the catch was that they
could move contaminated soil

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:25.443
as long as it served a function.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.150
And if you look at the permit for it,

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:33.150
there's no indication
that's actually storage

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.100
for polluted soil.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.143
It's just not in there.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.060
So this roundabout actually contains

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.190
really heavily polluted PFAS soil.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:59.100
So technically, it's
an illegal waste dump.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:01.233
But because it's already in here,

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.400
they're basically saying, oh,
you know, it's a done deal.

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.880
We're not going to bother, you know,

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.940
getting it out, if it's even possible.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:16.800
So, this is a whole problem,
you know, in this area

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:19.170
with the tunnel construction company,

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.910
is they're trying to create situations

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:24.003
where it's impossible to rectify.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.670
There was a public outcry.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:34.650
Activists then crowdfunded
to start testing

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:37.050
the bloodstream of certain residents

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:40.200
who lived near the factory for PFOS.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:45.200
And when those results
came out in August 2021,

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:51.240
it caused mayhem because
many of those people

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.790
that they tested, and just at random,

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:58.110
had incredibly high levels
of PFOS in their bloodstream.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:03.110
In one case, a woman in her 60s had levels

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:05.973
that were comparable to
industrial wastewater.

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:10.590
So 3M has been churning out varieties

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.953
of PFAS chemicals since the 1950s.

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:19.890
But it began doing studies in the '70s

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:22.650
that made them realize
that these chemicals

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.690
were highly toxic,

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:29.070
including two studies in
the late 1970s on monkeys,

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:34.070
which were disclosed as
part of a lawsuit in 2018.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:39.990
It was being sued for harming
the health of residents

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:43.173
of Minnesota who lived
near 3M's headquarters.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:50.550
They found high levels of
PFAS in drinking water,

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:54.930
particularly those people who
had wells on their property.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:58.770
And they noted higher rates of cancer

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:02.250
and leukemia in residents
that live nearby.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:05.310
In 2018, 3M agreed to settle a lawsuit

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:09.930
brought by the state of
Minnesota by paying $850 million

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.270
without admitting any wrongdoing.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.420
In 2000, 3M announced
it would stop producing

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:18.630
longer-chain PFAS as a
precautionary measure,

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:20.220
saying the chemicals were safe.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:23.160
But they announced that
they would be replacing them

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:27.600
with shorter-chain equivalents
that they said were safer.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:31.710
Those are now believed to be
potentially equally dangerous

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.870
to the environment and to human health

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.390
because they're highly
mobile and they spread

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:37.940
in the environment more easily.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.853
They try to project a, you know,

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:50.930
societal, corporate responsible view.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.530
But in the end, they've
known since the '80s

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:58.311
how toxic this product was.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.200
I think it's really disappointing

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:22.890
that 3M reached this
agreement to pay $580 million

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:24.420
to the Flemish government,

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:27.660
but so many of the
residents are left in limbo,

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:30.570
worried about their health,
worried about their kids,

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:32.760
worried about their house prices,

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.400
worried about their
surrounding environment.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.623
And very little has been done.

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:43.200
Now they say, don't play outside,

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.520
don't eat your vegetables.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:46.950
I'm like, hmm, it's your child.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.720
How I can tell my child, like,

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:52.440
please don't walk with your bare feet.

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:55.473
Don't touch the soil
because it's polluted.

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:57.480
It's impossible.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:15:00.330
And now I have to say,
don't touch that apple.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.940
Don't touch, don't do, it's poison.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:06.090
And then they're like, hmm, is it a fairy?

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.520
No, it's not a fairy. It's real life.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.800
We cannot eat those apples.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:11.940
It's poison.

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:12.773
Don't touch.

